WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Beside stores editable coding preferences alongside personal notes on your Mac.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.450
In Connections, Codex is scoped to read only “How you write”—keeping People and private notes off-limits.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:10.750
Ask Codex to review retry_fetch.rs. It calls beside_recall over local MCP and reads the two approved rules.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.400
Codex applies your style immediately: risks first, explicit errors, and a concrete diff with no filler.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.500
Beside records the read in Connections so you can inspect exactly what Codex received.
